# shear-tide
# arthur
# one inward spiral riding a 2.35-lobe tide: where the tide passes, bands pinch to knife ridges; a quarter-turn away they open into broad grain-bearing banks; the pinch circulates as the spiral descends. calm rings at rim and hub; the eye is the pupil and the ball parks on the innermost calm ring
